// TEST: FA T24: runtime row-extent guard names the Blade binding (aborts)
// A computed row whose extent is only known at run time is guarded against the
// declared extent in both lanes (BL8006). The message names the binding: the
// interpreter used to spell it through the C++ rename table (a binding named
// `final`, a C++ keyword, is `final_` there, and a long REPL session could show
// a stale rename), so the two lanes could name one binding two ways. Both now
// use the Blade name.
let n = reduce([1, 2], (+))
let row = Float64(0..n)
let final: Array<Float64 like Idx<2>, Idx<4>> = [row, row]
// ABORT: BL8006
// ABORT: row [0] of 'final' has extent 3
